\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Termination rule and terminal outcome}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}

\p{A \strong{termination rule} is a stopping time #{T} with respect to the
public-history filtration. The rule may stop on a submitted answer, an
environment terminal signal, a declared failure, or a fixed horizon.}

\p{A \strong{terminal outcome} #{Y} is a measurable function of the completed
interaction and any post-termination environment state that the protocol is
allowed to inspect. The policy need not observe all fields of #{Y}.}

\p{Stopping times and terminal outcomes are standard finite-horizon control
objects; see \citef{murphy2024reinforcement}. FTIP states the measurability
boundary because a terminal test result may be valid training feedback without
being valid information for an earlier action.}
